From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:10:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-apple: send a shutdown notification at final shutdown on
 post-M4

The post-M4 disable only clears CC.EN, so the controller counts every
Linux shutdown as unsafe and runs its unclean-shutdown recovery at the
next start. That slows the boot loader's device stage and the first
seconds of I/O.

At the final system shutdown, request a normal shutdown (CC.SHN) and
wait for CSTS.SHST before the CC.EN clear. m1n1 does the same before it
hands the controller over. Reset, recovery and removal keep the current
path. If the firmware does not complete the notification within
shutdown_timeout (5 s by default), the driver warns and the CC.EN clear
still runs.

Measured on a J616s (T6040), SMART read from the udisks cache, the
same boot loader and userspace each time:

  shutdown by          power_cycles  unsafe_shutdowns  next boot:
                                                      kernel start / Hyprland ready
  without it           1247 -> 1248  353 -> 354        2.23 s / 8.8 s
  with this patch      1248 -> 1249  354 -> 354        0.96 s / 3.7 s

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit bb5037c204502632fe5106f842f484ed4ebdb07e)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index 1fbbdcdc7b..77367f8d8d 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -221,6 +221,7 @@ struct apple_nvme {
 	bool abort_reset;
 	bool recover_to_live;
 	bool suspended;
+	bool final_shutdown;
 	unsigned long recovery_flags;
 
 	void __iomem *mmio_coproc;
@@ -1308,7 +1309,18 @@ static int apple_nvme_disable_locked(struct apple_nvme *anv, bool shutdown)
 	 * CFS and firmware crashes are not DMA fences. Post-M4 does not use
 	 * Delete SQ/CQ, SHN or RTKit sleep; only a completed CC.EN clear makes
 	 * the queue and request mappings eligible for release.
+	 *
+	 * The final system shutdown is the exception for SHN: without it the
+	 * controller counts every Linux shutdown as unsafe (SMART
+	 * unsafe_shutdowns) and recovers on the next start, which slows the
+	 * loader and the first seconds of I/O. A failed SHN changes nothing:
+	 * the CC.EN clear below still runs.
 	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(anv->final_shutdown) && !apple_rtkit_is_crashed(anv->rtk)) {
+		ret = nvme_disable_ctrl(&anv->ctrl, true);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(anv->dev, "shutdown notification failed: %d\n", ret);
+	}
 	ret = nvme_disable_ctrl(&anv->ctrl, false);
 	if (ret) {
 		apple_nvme_quarantine(anv, ret);
@@ -2535,6 +2547,7 @@ static void apple_nvme_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct apple_nvme *anv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
 	WRITE_ONCE(anv->removing, true);
+	WRITE_ONCE(anv->final_shutdown, true);
 	apple_nvme_set_reset_ready(anv, false);
 	flush_delayed_work(&anv->flush_dwork);
 	if (apple_nvme_disable(anv, true))
